  "drawn": true,
  "how": "The Apartment Subdistrict is the area the legend hatches with forward-leaning diagonals over MUR; the Metzger Business Subdistrict is hatched the other way. Each pixel was classed by a 45-degree run detector (forward minus backward diagonal density), the forward-hatched region filled and vectorised, mapped back to feet through the registration, and grown 15 ft so the edge sits on the map's black boundary line (about three pixels thick) rather than inside it. A lot the line cuts through stays unanswered (flats.geom.drawn).",
